Project: Django. Upgrade: 3.2 -> 4.2. Release of these items: 4.1.
Source: Django 4.1 release notes.

Label every item:
- risk = the change could break an application or deployment, require migration work, or create operational risk for SOME user upgrading across this release (removed or renamed APIs/settings/flags, changed defaults, behavior changes, raised minimum versions of runtimes/databases/dependencies, data or schema migration, required config changes, deprecated-and-removed features).
- context = accurate and useful but needs no user action at this release: explicitly "no user action required", a deprecation that still works (warning only), a purely additive new feature or option, documentation pointers.
- noise = credits, install/download commands, pure bug fixes that cannot change correct behavior, marketing text, headings with no content.

Return one label per item_id with a one-sentence reason grounded in the item text.

Items (JSON lines):
{"item_id": "b2caa89fd56d", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / django.contrib.postgres", "text": "ExclusionConstraint now supports covering exclusion constraints using SP-GiST indexes on PostgreSQL 14+."}
{"item_id": "42fe562d0bfe", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / django.contrib.postgres", "text": "The new default_bounds attribute of DateTimeRangeField and DecimalRangeField allows specifying bounds for list and tuple inputs."}
{"item_id": "ebc2579427f6", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / django.contrib.postgres", "text": "ExclusionConstraint now allows specifying operator classes with the OpClass() expression."}
{"item_id": "4fb250ab2261", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / django.contrib.sitemaps", "text": "The default sitemap index template <sitemapindex> now includes the <lastmod> timestamp where available, through the new get_latest_lastmod method. Custom sitemap index templates should be updated for the adjusted context variables."}
{"item_id": "6889aef93636", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / django.contrib.staticfiles", "text": "ManifestStaticFilesStorage now replaces paths to CSS source map references with their hashed counterparts."}
{"item_id": "78f2a18807ef", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Database backends", "text": "Third-party database backends can now specify the minimum required version of the database using the DatabaseFeatures.minimum_database_version attribute which is a tuple (e.g. (10, 0) means \"10.0\"). If a minimum version is specified, backends must also implement DatabaseWrapper.get_database_version(), which returns a tuple of the current database version. The backend's DatabaseWrapper.init_connection_state() method must call super() in order for the check to run."}
{"item_id": "4c3e088921ae", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Forms", "text": "The default template used to render forms when cast to a string, e.g. in templates as {{ form }}, is now configurable at the project-level by setting form_template_name on the class provided for FORM_RENDERER. Form.template_name is now a property deferring to the renderer, but may be overridden with a string value to specify the template name per-form class. Similarly, the default template used to render formsets can be specified via the matching formset_template_name renderer attribute."}
{"item_id": "6225dba30e92", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Forms", "text": "The new div.html form template, referencing Form.template_name_div attribute, and matching Form.as_div method, render forms using HTML <div> elements. This new output style is recommended over the existing as_table, as_p and as_ul styles, as the template implements <fieldset> and <legend> to group related inputs and is easier for screen reader users to navigate. The div-based output will become the default rendering style from Django 5.0."}
{"item_id": "360636040d2b", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Forms", "text": "In order to smooth adoption of the new <div> output style, two transitional form renderer classes are available: django.forms.renderers.DjangoDivFormRenderer and django.forms.renderers.Jinja2DivFormRenderer, for the Django and Jinja2 template backends respectively. You can apply one of these via the FORM_RENDERER setting. For example: FORM_RENDERER = \"django.forms.renderers.DjangoDivFormRenderer\" Once the <div> output style is the default, from Django 5.0, these transitional renderers will be deprecated, for removal in Django 6.0. The FORM_RENDERER declaration can be removed at that time."}
{"item_id": "e76c02e71378", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Forms", "text": "If the new <div> output style is not appropriate for your project, you should define a renderer subclass specifying form_template_name and formset_template_name for your required style, and set FORM_RENDERER accordingly. For example, for the <p> output style used by as_p, you would define a form renderer setting form_template_name to \"django/forms/p.html\" and formset_template_name to \"django/forms/formsets/p.html\"."}
{"item_id": "95ca0d1c28c3", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Forms", "text": "The new legend_tag allows rendering field labels in <legend> tags via the new tag argument of label_tag."}
{"item_id": "0a62c598404f", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Forms", "text": "The new edit_only argument for modelformset_factory and inlineformset_factory allows preventing new objects creation."}
{"item_id": "ddfc258ea945", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Forms", "text": "The js and css class attributes of Media now allow using hashable objects, not only path strings, as long as those objects implement the html() method (typically when decorated with the html_safe decorator)."}
{"item_id": "49df4de0c190", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Forms", "text": "The new BoundField.use_fieldset and Widget.use_fieldset attributes help to identify widgets where its inputs should be grouped in a <fieldset> with a <legend>."}
{"item_id": "b0d8cb041f41", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Forms", "text": "The formsets-error-messages argument for BaseFormSet now allows customizing error messages for invalid number of forms by passing 'too_few_forms' and 'too_many_forms' keys."}
{"item_id": "170e82846c32", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Forms", "text": "IntegerField, FloatField, and DecimalField now optionally accept a step_size argument. This is used to set the step HTML attribute, and is validated on form submission."}
{"item_id": "b51989a86f49", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Internationalization", "text": "The i18n_patterns function now supports languages with both scripts and regions."}
{"item_id": "8b66440cf339", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Management Commands", "text": "makemigrations --no-input now logs default answers and reasons why migrations cannot be created."}
{"item_id": "d9b32c65d652", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Management Commands", "text": "The new makemigrations --scriptable option diverts log output and input prompts to stderr, writing only paths of generated migration files to stdout."}
{"item_id": "b54f1e7dd5ad", "section": "What's new in Django 4.1 / Minor features / Management Commands", "text": "The new migrate --prune option allows deleting nonexistent migrations from the django_migrations table."}
